Inversion of Control (IoC)


-> What is IoC?

IoC means:
You don’t create objects — Spring creates and manages them.
Control of object creation is inverted from developer to container.



-> How Spring Implements IoC
   Uses IoC Container
   Reads configuration (XML / Annotations / Java Config)
   Creates objects (beans)
   Injects dependencies


-> Benefits of IoC
Loose coupling
Easy testing
Better maintenance
Clean architecture